title: Ishikawa Diagram
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
tags: MermaidExample

An Ishikawa diagram (fishbone or cause-and-effect diagram) maps the root causes of a problem across major categories, each shown as a branch off a central spine. Use it for root-cause analysis, quality improvement, and retrospective planning. ''New in Mermaid 11.'' Uses `ishikawa-beta`.

---

!! Basic example

```
ishikawa-beta
    Service Outage
    Infrastructure
        Database overload
        Network failure
    Code
        Memory leak
        Unhandled exception
    Process
        No monitoring
        Missing runbook
```

