!! Real-world example: Production deployment failure root-cause analysis

This example maps the causes of a failed production deployment across six standard quality categories (the "6M" framework: Machine, Method, Material, Measurement, Man, Mother Nature). The effect appears at the arrowhead; each category becomes a branch; subcauses nest under their category.

```
ishikawa-beta
    accTitle: Production deployment failure
    accDescr: Ishikawa fishbone diagram analysing root causes of a production deployment failure

    %% ── Effect (problem) ───────────────────────────
    Production Deployment Failed

    %% ── Cause categories ───────────────────────────
    Machine
        Build server out of disk
        CI pipeline timeout
        Container image corrupt

    Method
        No rollback procedure
        Missing deployment checklist
        Insufficient change approval

    Material
        Incompatible dependency version
        Config file missing from artifact
        Database migration not tested

    Measurement
        No smoke tests after deploy
        Alerting threshold too high
        Log level set to error only

    People
        On-call engineer unavailable
        Unclear ownership of service
        Insufficient deployment training

    Environment
        Network partition during deploy
        Load balancer misconfigured
        Staging environment diverged from prod
```

